=== CLARIFICATION of the four non-zero greps above ===
Every one is a COMMENT or an ERROR MESSAGE DISCLAIMING the thing, not code implementing it.
Verified by inspection:

  ReactionMechanism.hpp:19  "//     P18.5:  state + Arrhenius       ->  q"
  ReactionMechanism.hpp:14  "// WHAT THIS IS NOT: kinetics. Nothing here knows about A, n, Ea or
                             exp()."
  ReactionMechanism.cpp:203 "Stoichiometry is NOT renormalised to repair this -- the reaction is
                             refused."   (the mass-unbalance REJECTION message)
  ReactionMechanism.cpp:374 "DIAGNOSTIC ONLY. Nothing is clamped and no step is taken"

So: NO Arrhenius kinetics, NO exp(), NO renormalisation, NO clamping.

The greps are recorded AS RUN rather than tightened to exclude comments, because a grep that skips
comments could also skip a real occurrence. Reporting the raw count and resolving it by inspection
is the safer direction.

